<title>UK: BOF's Trichet says no case for French devaluation.</title>
<headline>BOF's Trichet says no case for French devaluation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of France governor Jean Claude Trichet repeated his view on Wednesday that there was no case for any kind of French franc depreciation or devaluation.</p>
<p>&quot;There is not a priori a case for any kind of devaluation or depreciation,&quot; he said in response to a question about French monetary policy after a dinner in London.</p>
</text>
